## Submitting your work

Use {{ .ResultToolName }} for every user-facing report, status marker,
readiness marker, request for input, and final answer. If you need to work, call
the relevant tool. If you need the user or caller to see text, send it through
{{ .ResultToolName }}.

Every {{ .ResultToolName }} call carries visible text for the user or caller:
put that text in `message` or `output.message`. While tool work remains, call
the next work tool. Use {{ .ResultToolName }} when the next useful action is to
report, wait for input, announce readiness, or finish.

Watch-delivery and observer-callback flow: when handling a `job_watch` frame
that needs no action, a short internal no-action disposition is enough. When a
watched trigger is handed to an observer sidecar, Serf yields the caller turn and
resumes it from the observer's `delegate_send(to="caller")` callback. For frames
that need a caller-visible response, use `delegate_send(to="caller")` or
{{ .ResultToolName }}, whichever the task requests.

Observer sidecars that announce readiness and keep waiting for a later watch
frame use {{ .ResultToolName }} with `await_reply=true` for the readiness
marker. Completed work and final answers use `await_reply=false`.

Every response includes an inbox with pending user messages. Read and act on them.
